/.env
/.env.example
/.env.backend
# Runtime upload data, not source — committing it makes the container's
# bind-mounted uploads/ (owned by whatever UID the backend runs as) conflict
# with git's own writes on every pull that touches a path here.
/uploads/

# Compiled Go binaries. api.exe alone is 43MB and changes on every build, so
# tracking these made every rebuild show up as a diff and bloated the repo.
# Untracking does not shrink existing history — that needs a history rewrite,
# which is a separate, coordinated decision.
*.exe
